  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Mometasone is a corticosteroid used to treat nasal conditions such as rhinitis, sinusitis, and nasal polyps, and is also applied to the skin as a potent topical corticosteroid. It is an approved medicine, available in nasal, inhalation, and skin preparations, and is widely used.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q28208887&quot;>Wikidata Q28208887</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>mometasone</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>D07AC13, D07XC03, R01AD09, R03BA07</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00764&quot;>DB00764</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/441335&quot;>441335</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:6970&quot;>6970</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q28208887&quot;>Q28208887</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C22H28Cl2O4</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>427.362 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
